### 4.3 index-service — NOT PINNED, so the shipped set is not knowable from this repo

`index-service/bootstrap.sh` installs with
`pip3 install --break-system-packages --ignore-installed -r requirements.txt`
on the index host. Only the four direct dependencies in §2 are exact-pinned;
**everything they pull in floats to whatever the resolver picks on the day the
host bootstraps.** That is a reproducibility hole as much as a licence one: two
hosts bootstrapped a week apart can run different code.

No transitive versions are stated here, because none can be stated honestly —
inventing them would be worse than admitting the gap. `index-service/requirements.lock`
has been added as a placeholder that must be filled from a verified build; until
then there is no authoritative manifest for this component.

For scope, the first-level requirements of the four pins, read from those exact
versions' core metadata (names only — the versions that ship are unknown, and
therefore so are their licences):

| Pinned package | Requires (first level, non-extra) |
| --- | --- |
| `mcp==1.23.3` | `anyio>=4.5`, `httpx>=0.27.1`, `httpx-sse>=0.4`, `jsonschema>=4.20.0`, `pydantic>=2.11.0,<3.0.0`, `pydantic-settings>=2.5.2`, `pyjwt[crypto]>=2.10.1`, `python-multipart>=0.0.9`, `sse-starlette>=1.6.1`, `starlette>=0.27`, `typing-extensions>=4.9.0`, `typing-inspection>=0.4.1`, `uvicorn>=0.31.1` |
| `uvicorn==0.44.0` | `click>=7.0`, `h11>=0.8` |
| `openpyxl==3.1.5` | `et-xmlfile` |
| `typing_extensions==4.15.0` | (none) |

`et-xmlfile` is a concrete example of what is missing: it is installed on every
index host and appears nowhere in this manifest, at no known version.

